## Context
DESIGN.md §4 item 7 and §3. Each experiment runs BEFORE its dependent and
carries a decision rule, not a hope — the rules live once, in DESIGN.md §3;
this ticket carries the work, the substrate, and the ordering. Drivers extend
bench/ and the 0008 harness; artifacts land in bench/results/ with
provenance, per house rules.
- X1 vector layout + int8: contiguous slab scan vs per-row at 100k/650k;
  stored-norm dot; int8 recall@30 at pools 2/8/32xk. Feeds the sidecar work
  in the scoped-issue machinery.
- X2 stopword-less OR latency at 650k, for the stopwords follow-up (0014).
- X3 monster RSS, in two honest halves (Copilot round 3: the streamed slab
  chunker it originally measured is unowned pre-RFC code). X3a, runnable
  before any new code: baseline RSS of stock upstream on the uncapped
  44.9 MB doc — reproduces 0011's 2 084,9 MiB class and feeds the rss-gate
  fixture (0026). X3b, the streamed-slab measurement with the 500 MB rule,
  runs when that chunker exists — it is built with scoped issue B's
  machinery (0034) and X3b travels with it, not with a pre-RFC ticket.
- X4 json_each constrained-MATCH cost at 1k/5k/20k/100k rowids on the 477k
  corpus, for the query-semantics work riding scoped issue A (0033).
- X5 segmenter seg/1 over the real 44.9 MB extraction (built by 0028).
  GATES scoped issue B (0034).
- X6 version-0 dynamics: re-extract one attachment on a synced and a
  never-synced profile; watch the census and the item version. Rule: if
  re-extraction re-stamps 0, build the bounded re-verify sweep; if anything
  observable bumps, the md5-widened signal suffices and the sweep is never
  built. Empirical annex to I-1 (0024).
- X7 census parse cost at 30k entries. Rule: > 50 ms -> cadence backs off to
  every 5th tick.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] each X EXCEPT X3b has a committed artifact in bench/results/ with
      provenance (X3b is owned by 0034's machinery and travels with it —
      excluding it here is what keeps 0025 closable before 0034, so the
      X5 -> 0034 gate is not circular)
- [ ] each decision rule evaluated in writing here (ship / fallback / never-build)
- [ ] no dependent (0026, 0033, 0034) proceeds past its gate before its X lands

## Substrate map (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
The corpora are NOT in the repo: bench/results/ holds JSON summaries; the
93,022 real vectors (343 MB sqlite) and the 477k-passage index live on the
author's machine (host doudou, /home/haduong/...), and the 44.9 MB extraction
is reachable only through the author's live Zotero. Per experiment:
- container-runnable today: X7; X4 if honestly rescoped to a synthetic 477k
  corpus (the cost curve's shape is structural — say so in the artifact);
  X1's layout/scan-timing half (vec_scaling.mjs is synthetic, needs sqlite-vec).
- author's machine required: X2 (650k FTS index), X3a (real 44.9 MB doc;
  X3b's streamed-slab chunker is owned by scoped issue B's machinery, 0034),
  X5 (real extraction + a human checking 50 cuts + seg/1 itself,
  built by 0028), X6 (two live Zotero profiles), and X1's int8-recall half
  (the anisotropy a symmetric synthetic fixture cannot exhibit —
  real-93022.json says why).
Preconditions: 0030 (bench drivers still set the pre-v1.7 env var — until it
lands, X2/X4 re-measurement silently measures `auto`); 0028 before X5.
Political review: check zotero#6012's state before spending X5 — structured
extraction upstream obsoletes the segmenter bet first.
